00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.913
- [Reader] In Blackwater
Woods, by Mary Oliver.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.660
Look, the trees are
turning their own bodies

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.193
into pillars of light,

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:53.790
are giving off the rich
fragrance of cinnamon

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:54.623
and fulfillment,

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:59.260
the long tapers of cattails are bursting

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:02.713
and floating away over the
blue shoulders of the ponds,

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.840
and every pond, no
matter what its name is,

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.543
is nameless now.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.010
Every year everything I have ever learned

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:19.260
in my lifetime leads back to this.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.740
The fires and the black river of loss

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.760
whose other side is salvation,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.893
whose meaning none of us will ever know.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:35.320
To live in this world you must be able

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.070
to do three things.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:40.403
To love what is mortal,

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.890
to hold it against your bones knowing

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.223
your own life depends on it,

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:52.160
and, when the time comes to let it go,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.243
to let it go.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.313
- We will be reading from
the First Covenant, Psalm 90.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:23.600
I will read the first line,

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.263
and we'd ask you to respond
in the italicized lines.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:40.110
Lord, you have been our dwelling
place in all generations.

00:08:42.125 --> 00:08:44.716
- [Audience] Before the
mountains were brought forth,

00:08:44.716 --> 00:08:48.369
or ever you had formed
the earth and the world,

00:08:48.369 --> 00:08:52.220
from everlasting to
everlasting you are God.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.537
- You turn us back to dust, and say,

00:08:54.537 --> 00:08:56.733
"Turn back, O mortal ones."

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.860
- [Audience] For a thousand
years in your sight

00:09:00.754 --> 00:09:02.504
are like yesterday when it is past,

00:09:03.707 --> 00:09:06.130
or as a watch in the night.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.750
- You sweep them away.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.370
They are like a dream,

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.313
like grass which is
renewed in the morning.

00:09:13.588 --> 00:09:16.430
- [Audience] In the morning
it flourishes and is renewed,

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:19.620
in the evening it fades and withers.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.460
- Teach us to number our days

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:25.113
that we may receive a heart of wisdom.

00:09:26.781 --> 00:09:28.479
- [Audience] Satisfy us in the morning

00:09:28.479 --> 00:09:30.656
with your steadfast love,

00:09:30.656 --> 00:09:34.520
so that we may rejoice
and be glad all our days.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.600
- Let the favor of the
Lord our God be upon us,

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.230
and establish the work
of our hands, together.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:44.973
- [All] O Lord, establish
the work of our hands.

00:09:46.329 --> 00:09:47.162
- Amen.

00:10:00.423 --> 00:10:03.340
(soft cello music)

00:10:07.076 --> 00:10:10.909
(singing in foreign language)

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:29.123
- The Continuous Life, by Mark Strand.

00:13:31.505 --> 00:13:34.380
What of the neighborhood
homes awash in a silver light,

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:37.140
of children hunched in the bushes,

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:41.260
watching for signs, the
grownups, for surrender,

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.450
signs that the irregular pleasures

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:45.420
of moving from day to day,

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.950
of being adrift on the swell of duty,

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:49.363
have run their course?

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:53.270
O parents, confess to your little ones

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.280
the night is a long way off

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:57.943
and your taste for the mundane grows.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:07.070
Tell them your worship of
household chores has barely begun.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:11.130
Describe the beauty of shovels
and rakes, brooms and mops.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.260
Say there will always be
cooking and cleaning to do,

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:18.470
that one thing leads to
another, which leads to another.

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:21.780
Explain that you live
between two great darks,

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:25.570
the first With an ending,
the second without one.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:28.460
That the luckiest thing
is having been born,

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:31.920
that you live in a blur of hours and days,

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:35.480
months and years, and
believe it has meaning,

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:38.940
despite the occasional
fear you are slipping away

00:14:40.027 --> 00:14:43.073
with nothing completed,
nothing to prove you existed.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.470
Tell the children to come inside,

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:49.630
that your search goes on
for something you lost,

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:52.430
a name, a family album that fell

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:55.620
from its own small matter into another,

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.950
a piece of the dark that
might have been yours,

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.970
you don't really know.

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:03.340
Say that each of you tries to keep busy,

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:07.820
learning to lean down close
and hear the casual breathing

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:12.240
of earth and feel its available
languor come over you,

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:16.910
wave after wave, sending
small tremors of love

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.360
through your brief, undeniable selves,

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:22.733
into your lives, and beyond.

00:15:35.783 --> 00:15:36.616
- Uh-oh.

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:38.523
My bad.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.310
Let us remember and give thanks

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:49.830
for those of our classmates who have died

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:53.463
and who blessed us by their
presence in our lives.

