00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.663
Is Elga's daughter Lauren with us?

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:22.690
- It's truly been a transformative weekend

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:23.913
to be here with you all.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:29.860
I hope you'll bear with
me for a few minutes

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.090
in this wonderful ceremony

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:34.690
so I can tell you a little
bit more about my mother.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:41.083
My mother lived her early
life in Berlin, Germany.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:46.043
To understand my mother, truly,

00:19:46.043 --> 00:19:47.693
you had to understand her mother.

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:53.820
She was an amazing woman, Lisa Steinherz.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:01.250
As early as 1930, she
realized that the family

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:04.050
would eventually need to leave Germany,

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.593
and she started to plan.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:12.720
Part of that planning included
hiring a British governess

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:17.750
for my mother and her younger brother

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:23.590
so that by the time she came to America

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:28.590
in 1936, at the age of 12,

00:20:28.924 --> 00:20:30.470
she was fluent in English.

00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:32.793
She had learned English in three years.

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:39.763
I read from her journal.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:46.270
1933 came into my sheltered
middle-class childhood

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:47.913
as a welcome diversion.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:53.530
My parents, suddenly preoccupied
with daily developments

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:57.000
for the first time, more or
less abandoned my brother

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.437
and me to the care of our
(speaking in foreign language).

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:05.393
Only she now stood between
me and independence.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:10.240
I still vividly recall
the pleasure I derived

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.373
by not eating what she put on my plate.

00:21:14.704 --> 00:21:17.440
By playing hide and go
seek, leading the poor girl

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:20.960
to believe me lost, and
by defying the bedtime

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.863
that had been rigidly
established by my mother.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:30.150
My brother and I sensed an air
of excitement in the house.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:43.303
She started school at a Montessori,

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:47.403
which was eventually closed by the Nazis.

00:21:49.451 --> 00:21:51.130
When the Montessori
school was ordered closed

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:54.030
shortly after Hitler came to power,

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:56.640
I was enrolled in an elementary school run

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.960
by the Jewish community of Berlin.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.810
I was thrilled.

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:04.730
This was real school at
last, formal classrooms,

00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:09.023
regular recess, grades,
and above all, homework.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:11.580
On the way home from school,

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:14.623
I passed billboards with
anti-Semitic cartoons.

00:22:15.550 --> 00:22:17.150
My good friend Susie and I

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:21.610
were inseparable 12 year olds in 1936.

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:25.340
Quite accustomed to being
barred from our favorite parks

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:28.313
by signs proclaiming, for Aryans only.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.820
By the time we arrived
after a six-day crossing

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:37.253
of the Atlantic, I was delighted
to step ashore in New York.

00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:43.760
Susie went to England rather than America,

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:48.143
and an active correspondence was begun.

00:22:50.461 --> 00:22:51.803
September 1937.

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:54.840
Dear Susie, I hope you don't think

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:57.410
that I've forgotten you,
but since I am in school,

00:22:57.410 --> 00:22:59.450
there is very little time to write.

00:22:59.450 --> 00:23:02.640
The high school is prima, first class.

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:05.170
I have the choice of
taking the academic course

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:06.620
or the general course.

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:08.350
I will take the academic course,

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:10.370
because I want to go to college.

00:23:10.370 --> 00:23:12.740
Because of this, I will
take French and Latin

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:14.883
instead of typing and stenography.

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:18.560
I was able to choose
between painting and music.

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:20.610
I chose music.

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:23.940
I will also take English,
mathematics, physics,

00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:26.520
and social studies, that is,

00:23:26.520 --> 00:23:29.913
geography, history,
politics, all mixed together.

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:45.070
Virgina Woolf wrote, for we
think back through our mothers,

00:23:46.390 --> 00:23:47.563
if we are women.

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:56.107
Helen Epstein wrote the
book, "Where She Came From,"

00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:00.113
about her mother's
experiences in the Holocaust.

00:24:02.678 --> 00:24:04.683
I always felt protective of my mother,

00:24:05.855 --> 00:24:08.403
because she had lost so
many friends and family.

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:12.120
I imagined what it must have been like,

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:16.510
because she hardly ever talked about it.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.233
She said she didn't remember.

00:24:20.550 --> 00:24:21.873
Helen Epstein wrote,

00:24:24.580 --> 00:24:26.860
I wore the clothes my mother made for me,

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:28.660
read the books she read,

00:24:28.660 --> 00:24:30.920
valued what she thought good.

00:24:30.920 --> 00:24:34.130
I shared my life with her for a long time,

00:24:34.130 --> 00:24:37.150
long after adolescence
should have ruptured the bond

00:24:37.150 --> 00:24:40.020
between us, I shared her loves,

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:43.370
her disappointments, and her memories.

00:24:43.370 --> 00:24:46.680
She was the engine behind my energy,

00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:51.460
my defender when I needed one, my solace.

00:24:51.460 --> 00:24:54.193
When the break finally
came, it was brutal.

00:24:55.250 --> 00:24:58.006
We came apart in a great explosion

00:24:58.006 --> 00:25:00.523
that required years to repair.

00:25:04.490 --> 00:25:06.680
In her last years, my mother lived

00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:09.950
in a retirement community in Lexington,

00:25:09.950 --> 00:25:12.583
while my father was sinking into dementia.

00:25:13.870 --> 00:25:18.560
It was during that time and
while I was living close by

00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:20.363
that my mother and I rejoined.

00:25:21.450 --> 00:25:23.993
We had a standing Tuesday dinner date.

00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:28.316
Sometimes I picked up
my young granddaughter,

00:25:28.316 --> 00:25:33.000
her great-granddaughter,
Ellaria, from daycare

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:35.170
and she joined us too.

00:25:35.170 --> 00:25:37.393
Our dinners were times of healing.

00:25:39.210 --> 00:25:42.423
My father died late in 2013.

00:25:43.490 --> 00:25:47.453
Shortly after, my mother
was diagnosed with cancer.

00:25:48.660 --> 00:25:53.660
Her last weeks were a gift
we shared with each other.

00:25:54.070 --> 00:25:57.680
In October 2014, I stayed

00:25:57.680 --> 00:26:00.123
with her while she received hospice care.

00:26:02.920 --> 00:26:06.910
She dictated these last thoughts to me

00:26:08.310 --> 00:26:12.870
as I sat in bed with her
and as I knit a layette

00:26:12.870 --> 00:26:15.993
for her soon to be born
second grand-daughter, Nadia.

00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:29.063
See if I can find it.

00:26:35.030 --> 00:26:36.943
November 2014.

00:26:39.010 --> 00:26:42.300
I would like my family and friends

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:46.300
to know that I am grateful
for the man I married

00:26:46.300 --> 00:26:47.883
and the parents I had.

00:26:49.470 --> 00:26:53.260
I could not be more appreciative
of my three children

00:26:53.260 --> 00:26:55.320
and my seven grandchildren,

00:26:55.320 --> 00:26:58.630
and my one great-grandchild, Ellaria,

00:26:58.630 --> 00:27:00.943
and my great-grandchild to come.

00:27:02.450 --> 00:27:06.370
I wish everyone could be
as lucky as I have been

00:27:07.270 --> 00:27:11.453
in having such a family
and such good friends.

00:27:12.720 --> 00:27:17.210
I am appreciative of Brookhaven,
where she was living.

00:27:17.210 --> 00:27:20.710
It has enriched the last years of my life

00:27:20.710 --> 00:27:23.113
with new friendships and activities.

00:27:24.410 --> 00:27:27.453
I have loved the times we
all spent in Wellfleet.

00:27:29.030 --> 00:27:31.680
I have had a very scattered career,

00:27:31.680 --> 00:27:35.386
but I enjoyed all phases of it,

00:27:35.386 --> 00:27:40.386
teacher, administrator,
lawyer, mediator, and writer.

00:27:45.030 --> 00:27:49.063
It is time for somebody my age to move on.

00:27:50.910 --> 00:27:55.910
I hope that all of you will
carry on the values I hold,

00:27:57.230 --> 00:28:02.230
peace and justice and equal
opportunity, Elga Wasserman.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:12.133
She's buried in Grove Street Cemetery.

00:28:13.283 --> 00:28:14.203
It's a beautiful spot.

00:28:15.518 --> 00:28:16.351
Thank you.

00:28:18.833 --> 00:28:21.583
(peaceful music)

00:31:08.070 --> 00:31:09.293
- We remember them.

00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:13.630
Please join for the responsive reading,

00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:15.163
the words in italics.

00:31:16.506 --> 00:31:19.047
This is by Roland Gittelsohn
in "The Gates of Prayer."

00:31:19.950 --> 00:31:21.530
In the rising of the sun,

00:31:21.530 --> 00:31:23.660
and in its going down.

00:31:23.660 --> 00:31:25.460
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:25.460 --> 00:31:27.120
- In the blowing of the wind

00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:28.990
and in the chill of winter.

00:31:28.990 --> 00:31:30.840
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:34.747
- In the opening buds and
in the rebirth of spring.

00:31:34.747 --> 00:31:36.460
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:36.460 --> 00:31:40.204
- In the blueness of the sky
and in the warmth of summer.

00:31:40.204 --> 00:31:42.130
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:42.130 --> 00:31:46.286
- In the rustling of leaves
and in the beauty of autumn.

00:31:46.286 --> 00:31:47.800
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:50.850
- In the beginning of the
year and when it ends.

00:31:50.850 --> 00:31:52.890
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:52.890 --> 00:31:56.109
- When we are weary and
in need of strength.

00:31:56.109 --> 00:31:57.293
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:31:57.293 --> 00:32:00.649
- When we are lost and sick at heart.

00:32:00.649 --> 00:32:01.993
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:32:01.993 --> 00:32:05.090
- When we have joys we yearn to share.

00:32:05.090 --> 00:32:07.160
- [Audience] We remember them.

00:32:07.160 --> 00:32:10.577
- So long as we live, they too shall live,

00:32:10.577 --> 00:32:12.273
for they are now a part of us.

00:32:13.490 --> 00:32:16.240
- [Audience] As we remember them.

00:32:33.120 --> 00:32:35.440
- Throughout the planning
of this celebration,

00:32:35.440 --> 00:32:37.930
we heard from several first women

00:32:37.930 --> 00:32:39.490
who could not join us today

00:32:39.490 --> 00:32:43.480
because of illness,
disability, or incapacity.

00:32:43.480 --> 00:32:48.433
Some are caregivers themselves
for partners and spouses.

00:32:49.740 --> 00:32:51.990
As we honor the memory
of those who have died,

00:32:51.990 --> 00:32:55.220
let us also remember those
in need of our support,

00:32:55.220 --> 00:32:58.453
in need of a kind word,
in need of a prayer.

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:02.550
As you let the beauty and
emotion fill your hearts

00:33:02.550 --> 00:33:04.720
during this song of healing,

00:33:04.720 --> 00:33:07.370
I invite you to send your
most loving of thoughts

00:33:07.370 --> 00:33:10.170
to those who could not be here,

00:33:10.170 --> 00:33:13.433
and pray their names quietly to yourself.

00:33:22.836 --> 00:33:25.419
(gentle music)

00:33:36.352 --> 00:33:40.185
(singing in foreign language)

00:33:58.319 --> 00:34:02.803
♪ May the source of strength ♪

00:34:02.803 --> 00:34:07.803
♪ Who blessed the ones before us ♪

00:34:10.036 --> 00:34:13.830
♪ Help us find the courage ♪

00:34:13.830 --> 00:34:18.830
♪ To make our lives a blessing ♪

00:34:19.534 --> 00:34:22.701
♪ And let us say amen ♪

00:34:44.417 --> 00:34:48.250
(singing in foreign language)

00:35:03.921 --> 00:35:08.895
♪ Bless those in need of healing with ♪

00:35:08.895 --> 00:35:12.728
(singing in foreign language)

00:35:14.794 --> 00:35:19.301
♪ The renewal of body ♪

00:35:19.301 --> 00:35:23.713
♪ The renewal of spirit ♪

00:35:23.713 --> 00:35:26.963
♪ And let us say, amen ♪

00:35:56.554 --> 00:35:57.387
- Amen.

00:35:59.840 --> 00:36:01.870
We are coming to the
close of this service,

00:36:01.870 --> 00:36:03.350
and I'd like to thank everyone

00:36:03.350 --> 00:36:05.890
who had a hand in its planning.

00:36:05.890 --> 00:36:08.620
The committee was hard at
work across many miles,

00:36:08.620 --> 00:36:10.430
but always, even at a distance,

00:36:10.430 --> 00:36:12.163
with love and care in mind.

00:36:13.300 --> 00:36:16.190
Thank you, as well, to all
those behind the scenes

00:36:16.190 --> 00:36:19.560
who handled logistics
and forgotten details.

00:36:19.560 --> 00:36:21.060
None of this would have been possible

00:36:21.060 --> 00:36:22.833
without your patient touch.

00:36:23.850 --> 00:36:26.200
Deep gratitude to our readers

00:36:26.200 --> 00:36:28.770
and incredible musicians.

00:36:28.770 --> 00:36:33.770
Nicoletta, Yun, beautiful
Martina, you blessed us.

00:36:34.370 --> 00:36:35.203
Thank you.

00:36:37.318 --> 00:36:39.518
Truly, you gave us balm
for our weary souls.

00:36:40.500 --> 00:36:43.720
Finally, to each one of you
gathered here this morning,

00:36:43.720 --> 00:36:47.170
thank you for coming, for
being present to each other

00:36:47.170 --> 00:36:50.890
while we lifted up the
names of Yale's first women

00:36:50.890 --> 00:36:51.793
who have died.

00:36:53.040 --> 00:36:54.980
As you journey out of this space

00:36:54.980 --> 00:36:57.900
into the throes of continuing celebration,

00:36:57.900 --> 00:37:00.570
and then back to your daily lives,

00:37:00.570 --> 00:37:03.400
remember the gift you were to Yale,

00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:05.750
and trust that your brave light

00:37:05.750 --> 00:37:09.263
and steadfast pursuit
of truth lives on today.

00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:12.260
Please know that you
are welcome to stay here

00:37:12.260 --> 00:37:14.090
as long as you may need.

00:37:14.090 --> 00:37:16.240
Continue to share stories.

00:37:16.240 --> 00:37:19.880
Continue to share your remarkable selves.

00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:22.150
May you imagine a tomorrow

00:37:22.150 --> 00:37:25.680
where memories of your
departed sisters rest safe

00:37:25.680 --> 00:37:28.970
and sheltered in the warmest of places,

00:37:28.970 --> 00:37:31.350
where hope is always abundant

00:37:31.350 --> 00:37:33.003
and sustaining to you.

00:37:34.170 --> 00:37:36.613
My friends, I bid you peace.

00:37:44.005 --> 00:37:48.005
(gentle cello and guitar music)

00:38:20.905 --> 00:38:25.905
♪ Amazing grace ♪

00:38:26.128 --> 00:38:30.979
♪ How sweet the sound ♪

00:38:30.979 --> 00:38:35.979
♪ That saved a wretch like me ♪

00:38:40.687 --> 00:38:45.687
♪ I once was lost but now I'm found ♪

00:38:50.150 --> 00:38:53.650
♪ Was blind but now I see ♪

00:39:00.374 --> 00:39:05.374
♪ Twas grace that taught
my heart to fear ♪

00:39:09.939 --> 00:39:13.772
♪ And grace my fears relieved ♪

00:39:20.479 --> 00:39:25.062
♪ O how precious did that grace appear ♪

00:39:31.139 --> 00:39:34.806
♪ The hour I first believed ♪

00:39:43.459 --> 00:39:48.459
♪ Through many dangers, toils and snares ♪

00:39:52.611 --> 00:39:55.778
♪ I have already come ♪

00:40:02.873 --> 00:40:07.706
♪ Tis grace that brought
me safe thus far ♪

00:40:12.879 --> 00:40:16.712
♪ And grace will lead me home ♪

00:40:25.408 --> 00:40:30.408
♪ Amazing grace ♪

00:40:32.569 --> 00:40:37.569
♪ Amazing grace ♪

00:40:40.636 --> 00:40:42.969
♪ How sweet ♪

00:40:52.762 --> 00:40:55.179
♪ Your sound ♪

00:41:16.430 --> 00:41:18.230
- Thank you so much.

00:41:18.230 --> 00:41:19.830
One last invitation.

00:41:19.830 --> 00:41:23.990
If you had written a
remembrance for a classmate,

00:41:23.990 --> 00:41:27.430
you are welcome to come
and take one candle.

00:41:27.430 --> 00:41:31.110
Please watch your step, but
we would love these candles

00:41:31.110 --> 00:41:34.060
to live in hope in your households.

00:41:34.060 --> 00:41:34.893
Thank you.

00:41:36.635 --> 00:41:39.218
(gentle music)

00:41:48.810 --> 00:41:51.727
(crowd chattering)

